      "type": "text",
      "text": "{\"pair_id\": \"Nefertiti|857151\", \"verdict\": \"different_name\", \"reasoning\": \"Record 2 reads as the signs n f r t, j y t j, n f r, n f r w, j t n. Nefertiti has the consonants n, f, r, t, t, with vowel letters e and i. It can match the first element Nfr.t (n, f, r, t, with the vowels as extras) and the t of jy.tj (the i's can stand for j and y or be dropped). But the transliteration also has nfr, nfr.w and Jtn: n, f, r, n, f, r, w and a final t and n. Record 1 has no letters to represent any of these, and the final n has nothing in the name. These signs are not ꞽ, j, y, w or an element-final t, so their absence makes the names different. The record 2 lemma is the full epithet name 'Nofretete, schön ist die Schönheit Atons', while record 1 is the short form Nefertiti.\"}"
